<!--meta {"lead": "The theme toggle switches the product between light and dark and remembers the choice, so a person who prefers dark at night is never flashed with white on the next page.", "description": "Pressed-state ghost button in the top bar; follows the system until chosen, then persists.", "pills": ["Toggle button (aria-pressed)", "Status: stable"], "variants": "one: ghost small button with a constant label", "states": "not pressed (light), pressed (dark), hover, focus, active", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/braider-requests/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every product shell (customer and braider) carries one theme toggle in the top bar (L2-048). It is a <a href="button.html">button</a> with the ghost variant and small size whose pressed state means "dark theme on". Without a saved choice the product follows <code>prefers-color-scheme</code>; once toggled, the choice is stored and applied before first paint.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy"><div class="ds-anatomy__figure"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Dark theme</button></div>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list"><li><div><b>Button</b><small><code>.btn.btn--ghost.btn--sm</code> with <code>aria-pressed</code>.</small></div></li><li><div><b>Label</b><small>Constant "Dark theme"; the pressed state, not the words, changes.</small></div></li></ol></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants" data-na="One variant: a pressed-state ghost button."><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2></section>
<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Small only, to sit beside the account link."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  {{themes}}<button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Dark theme</button><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Dark theme</button><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-state="focus">Dark theme</button>{{/themes}}
  <p>Not pressed, pressed and focused. Pressed uses the button's pressed styling.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul><li>Stays in the bar at every width, before the menu button on phones.</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Sets <code>data-theme="light|dark"</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> and stores the choice in essential storage under <code>hp-theme</code> (a functional preference, not optional usage data). An inline script in the document head applies the stored value before styles paint.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3><p>WAI-ARIA toggle button: native <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> with <code>aria-pressed</code>.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3><table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> / <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Switches the theme and flips the pressed state.</td></tr></tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3><p>Shared focus ring; focus stays on the button after switching.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3><p>"Dark theme, toggle button, pressed" or "not pressed". The label never changes, so the state is not announced twice.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">{{pair:Label|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}</div>
  <h3>Motion</h3><p>The theme switches instantly; no cross-fade.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3><p>44px target through the small button's padding.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul><li>Label: "Dark theme". Not "Toggle theme" or a glyph.</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Dark theme</button></div><figcaption>Constant label with a pressed state.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button">☀ Light</button></div><figcaption>A label that flips to the other theme, with a glyph, as in the mock chrome: is it the current theme or the next one?</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <p>Uses the button's ghost and pressed tokens; it adds none of its own.</p>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{tok:Label|--color-fg-default}}{{tok:Pressed background|--color-accent-subtle}}</tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false"&gt;Dark theme&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>{{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|customer top bar}}{{mock:pages/braider-requests/default|braider top bar}}</ul>
  <p>New in this revision: the first mocks had a theme switch only in the mock chrome, not in the product (L2-042 AC3, L2-048).</p>
</section>
